  "title": "# Build: drag-to-tab (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** Drag to tab · **Category:** Feature ## What …",
  "asked": "# Build: drag-to-tab (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** Drag to tab · **Category:** Feature ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"I want to be able to drag [items] to their containers and drop them as new tabs. Like grab something from the navigation menu, or from one tab, drag it over to another area and drop it as a new tab.\" Name confirmed: \"All right, yeah.\" Book to a free named agent. **Builds on molly-multi-instance-tabs (PR #328: + button, multi-instance tabs, hold-then-drag between tab groups) and tab-group-assets (#327).** If they haven't merged yet, branch from their branches or wait. Don't duplicate their work. ## Do 1. **Drag from any navigation menu item** (Molly nav, console nav, axHub/AmberX nav, collapsible app containers) and drop it onto any tab group / pane / container. It opens that screen/plugin/app **as a new tab** there (a new instance if it's already open elsewhere, per #328). 2. **Drop targets**: highlight valid tab groups and pane edges while dragging. Dropping on a tab strip inserts at that position. Dropping on a pane edge splits and creates a new tab group (dock@1). Dropping outside creates a floating window. 3. **Tab to tab group**: confirm #328's drag between groups works across apps and containers, including dragging a tab onto the nav menu to pin it as a nav item (optional; note it if skipped). 4. Phone: long-press then drag, with the same drop highlights. Undo after every drop. 5. Works in every app through the shared tab-group/dock components, not just Molly. 6. Basic Markdown readme. Tests, UI Review shots (non-blocking), PR **through the merge queue only** (auto-land is OFF). Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
